&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/www-yahoo&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3770446&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1607398546&quot; alt=&quot;www-yahoo&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3770446)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/www-yahoo&quot;  &gt;www-yahoo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-878908-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. For example, a request for a concept such as &amp;quot;happiness&amp;quot; will lead to slight fluctuations in circumstance for the benefit of the recipient of said &amp;quot;happiness,&amp;quot; while a wish for &amp;quot;beauty&amp;quot; will simply change the recipient&#039;s perception of themself as well as those around them rather than alter anything physically. (See documentation for tests 5133-227 and 5133-077 for more information.)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</description>
